<title>UK: Smith &amp; Nephew to market Dermagraft in Canada.</title>
<headline>Smith &amp; Nephew to market Dermagraft in Canada.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drug company Smith &amp; Nephew Plc said on Monday it and its U.S. partner had received approval to market Dermagraft in Canada for the treatment of diabetic foot ulcers.</p>
<p>Canada has some 1.5 million diabetics, of which about 7.5 percent will have a foot ulcer in their lifetime, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Smith &amp; Nephew teamed up with U.S-based Advanced Tissue Sciences Inc in April 1996 to commercialise Dermagraft.</p>
<p>The product uses living cells derived from babies' foreskins to grow on a naturally-absorbable scaffold across wounds.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
